Movement Conflict Rules

Use this rule set:

Stationary unit holds its tile.
Moving unit cannot enter a tile occupied by a stationary unit.
If multiple moving units attempt to enter the same empty tile, nobody moves.
If two moving units attempt to swap tiles, both fail.
No pushing.
No sliding.
No alternate path.
No random priority.
No hidden EntityId advantage for gameplay resolution unless used only as a final deterministic ordering tool for processing.
Definition of Stationary

A unit is stationary if it did not successfully move during the previous resolved movement tick.

